mary":"The assigned contracts align with the DEF, S2 acceptance criteria, HLD and current shared types. S1 retains coordination and authorization ownership; S2 supplies workflow and analysis measurements while preserving legacy execution contracts. No blocking defects were demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/contractDetails","/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/0","/body/hldContextSlice/consumedContracts/0","/body/hldContextSlice/consumedContracts/1","/body/hldContextSlice/consumedContracts/2","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/8","document:line:26","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S002/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s2.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: sections 3–6, especially S2 ac1–ac2","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md: sections 3, 5–8","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md: section 2.1","src/shared/task-progress.ts: TaskRefSchema, MeasuredCountSchema, DelegateMeasurement, TaskProgressDelegate and ProgressSnapshot","src/daemon/task-progress/coordinator.ts: registerProducer and normalize","src/daemon/task-progress/record.ts: validProgressMeasurement","src/daemon/task-progress/runtime.ts: openProgressRuntime","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: workflow stage mapping and token accumulator","src/daemon/workflow-run-registry.ts: detached execution callbacks and settlement","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts: runStart frame protocol","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md: legacy progress requirements","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md: legacy stream contract"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Replace citation c1's ambiguous reference “s1” with a durable bundle identifier or concrete source locations. Its substantive claim is supported by the inspected workflow and analysis code.","In the delegate signature, retain the shared type's D extends { readonly kind: ProgressKind } constraint to make the discriminant requirement explicit."]},{"chunkId":"adapters","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned adapter design aligns with S2 ac1/ac2 and the HLD. It covers streaming workflows, detached workflows and analysis while preserving legacy frames, results and cancellation authority. Measurement units and unknown counts are supported by the current producer code. No blocking defects were demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/testStrategy","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/10","/citations/11","document:line:84","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S002/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s2.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: constraints k1–k4, k7–k8 and S2 ac1–ac2","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md: architecture, sc4, S2 boundary and rollout","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md: legacy progress contracts and compatibility requirements","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:114–157, 219–276, 468–579, 640–647","src/daemon/workflow-run-registry.ts:124–221","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:579–886","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-run-registry.test.ts:104–248","src/analyze/orchestrator/types.ts:113–224","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:473–517","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts: task identity validation","src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:729–758","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts:259–306","src/workflow/executor.ts: runner registry and paused-step identity checks"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add a compact event-to-measurement table naming the phase allowlists, active-unit validation rules and clear/retain behavior. This would make the intended mapping easier to implement consistently.","Extend the proposed fixtures with nested analysis plans that reuse task IDs and a cached analysis completion. If analysis position counts are implemented, verify parentTaskPath isolation; also assert that controller steps and nested workflow grounding do not register additional tasks."]},{"chunkId":"lifecycle","status":"incomplete","summary":"The lifecycle design aligns with S2 requirements and the inspected daemon boundaries. It preserves independent legacy settlement, centralizes observation ownership, and covers fencing, quiet liveness, cancellation races and persistence failures. No demonstrated blocking defect was found. Mandatory verification of the generated sequence rendering could not be completed.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/companions","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/9","document:line:80","document:line:84","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S002/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s2.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/task-progress-workflow-analysis-s2-lld.json: completed contracts and adapters feedback","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: constraints and S2 acceptance criteria","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20